> I started a monk a minute ago. He explored level one, found a red ring
> and waited for his dog to curse-test it. The dog happily walked over
> the ring twice and my monk decided to get the jewelry.
>
> When the monk walked into the square, it activated a magic trap
> sending a column of flame from the floor killing him.
>
> How come my pet avoided the trap?

     Magic traps only have a small chance to affect monsters (for
any monster, not just a pet).  When nothing interesting happens,
there is no message nor is the trap revealed to you on the map,
but that trap type does become known to the monster.  After the
first time, your pet then had a 75% chance of escaping magic
traps (any magic trap, not just that one), so its chance to being
harmed the second time was extremely small (on the order of 1%).


